            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0301" n="189" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 21891/2.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chilean
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-02-24"><hi rendition="#italic">February 24,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 31.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of January 27, 1910,
                    numbered 2, inviting this Government to take part in the celebration of the
                    centennial anniversary of Chilean independence and to be represented in the
                    festivities commemorative thereof, the Department takes great pleasure in
                    informing you that the invitation is accepted.</p>
                <p>The Navy Department of the United States have arranged to have the First Division
                    of the Pacific Fleet, consisting of the <hi rendition="#italic">California, <pb
                            facs="0302" n="190" xml:id="pg190"/> South Dakota, Pennsylvania</hi>,
                    and <hi rendition="#italic">Colorado</hi>, armored cruisers, and the supply ship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Glacier</hi>, visit Valparaiso on the 18th of
                    September. The Department of State will instruct the United States delegates
                    which will be named to represent it at the Pan American Conference to proceed to
                    Santiago after the adjournment of said conference. This delegation will be
                    accredited to represent the United States at the celebration of the centennial
                    of Chilean independence.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Knox</hi></signed>),<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                            Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
